From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a shell started again shows the desktop in its own X window

The Wine desktop can outlive the shell that made its X window: a program
still running on it (a crashed one kept by its debugger, a tray program)
holds it. That X window dies with the shell. The shell started again made
its own X window (CreateDesktop) but then took the dead one the desktop
window still named: its first window failed with BadWindow, and so did
every restart, until the session gave up -- stuck at "Getting things
ready" (David 2026-10-01, field report item 9: after AmbirScan crashed the
desktop; on the QA VM, AmbirScan crashing as its X server went away during
a session restart did the same). Now a desktop X window that no longer
exists is replaced by the shell's own.

Proven on the QA VM (the restart that failed six times signs in now).
Gate: test/shellrestart-gate.sh checks the restart path; under Xvfb it
does not reach the dead-window state, so the mutant
SG_MUTANT_STALE_DESKTOP passes it (known gap).
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -2588,6 +2588,22 @@
 }
 
 
+static int desktop_exists_error( Display *display, XErrorEvent *event, void *arg )
+{
+    return 1;
+}
+
+/* whether the X window still exists (it belonged to another process, which may be gone) */
+static BOOL desktop_window_exists( Window win )
+{
+    XWindowAttributes attr;
+    BOOL ok;
+
+    X11DRV_expect_error( gdi_display, desktop_exists_error, NULL );
+    ok = XGetWindowAttributes( gdi_display, win, &attr ) != 0;
+    return !X11DRV_check_error() && ok;
+}
+
 /* initialize the desktop window id in the desktop manager process */
 static BOOL create_desktop_win_data( Window win, HWND hwnd )
 {
@@ -2655,6 +2671,22 @@
     else
     {
         Window win = (Window)NtUserGetProp( hwnd, whole_window_prop );
+        if (win && win != root_window && is_virtual_desktop() && !desktop_window_exists( win ))
+        {
+            /* Stained Glass OS: the desktop outlived the shell that made its
+             * X window -- a program still running on it (a crashed one kept
+             * by its debugger, a tray program) -- and that window died with
+             * the shell. This shell has just made its own (CreateDesktop):
+             * the desktop is shown in that one now. Taking the dead one, the
+             * shell's first window failed (BadWindow) and every restart with
+             * it: the session never got past "Getting things ready" (David
+             * 2026-10-01: after AmbirScan crashed the desktop). */
+            WARN( "desktop window %lx is gone, using %lx\n", win, root_window );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_STALE_DESKTOP
+            create_desktop_win_data( root_window, hwnd );
+            return;
+#endif
+        }
         if (win && win != root_window) X11DRV_init_desktop( win, width, height );
     }
 }
